cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying paper, please cite them. This is a preprint-stage research codebase; it has not been peer reviewed and is not a medical device."
title: "CARDION: simulated-event and spiking heart-rate estimators versus frame-based rPPG on real webcam video"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Mullen"
    given-names: "Jacob"
license: MIT
abstract: "Research code, trained models, saved results and manuscript for a subject-disjoint study of whether events emulated from compressed webcam video preserve the pulse, whether a spiking neural network helps, and how a reliability gate affects reported accuracy and availability. Events are simulated; no event-camera hardware is used."
keywords:
  - remote photoplethysmography
  - event camera
  - spiking neural network
  - simulated events
  - heart rate
  - reliability gating
  - reproducibility

repository-code: https://github.com/mullenjacob/CARDION
url: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23647425
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23647425
